# Raw downloads and the cleaned match table are both fully reproducible by
# running `python -m src.collect && python -m src.clean`. The cleaned file is
# ~19 MB and would be rewritten every week, so committing it would add roughly
# a gigabyte of history per year for no information gain.
data/raw/
data/processed/

# output/ IS committed on purpose. Those are the predictions, and their git
# history is the proof they were not edited after the matches were played.
